<title>USA: Banco Santander ups Chile affiliate stake.</title>
<headline>Banco Santander ups Chile affiliate stake.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-06-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Spain's Banco Santander SA said Wednesday it had purchased an additional 3.5 percent of Banco Santander-Chile.</p>
<p>This purchase brings Banco Santander's holding in Banco Santander-Chile to 78.15 percent, the company said.</p>
<p>The shares were purchased from Infisa and former shareholders of Banco Osorno y la Union, which merged with Banco Santander-Chile last year.</p>
<p>The additional stake was purchased for US$62 million, or US$15.50 per ADR.</p>
<p>Banco Santander Chile's net income for 1996 was US$95.1 million.</p>
<p>Grupo Santander is the marketing name for Spain's Banco Santender SA.</p>
</text>
